author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "A context assembly separates its state-derived part from its asker-derived part, and the state-derived part is addressed by a fingerprint over every input that can change it, enumerated in contract data rather than in code comments; Two agents issuing the same request against an unchanged workspace receive byte-identical shared assemblies and the second is served from the cache, proven by a test asserting one computation and two served results; The fingerprint is proven complete by a negative-control fixture per declared input: changing that input alone must change the address, so a stale assembly can never be served as fresh; The cache is a keyed store rather than a single slot, so distinct legitimate request shapes coexist instead of evicting each other, directly refuting the failure mode pm-77okxr records; A fleet-level token budget is declarable and observable: aggregate context spend across agents is reported over a window, and exceeding the target degrades deterministically by the same declared ladder a single command uses; Every served assembly carries its attestation, so a consumer can verify the shared part was produced by the inputs it claims without recomputing it; Amortization degenerates exactly to today's behaviour for a single agent on a small workspace, adding no cache lookup cost that a one-agent workspace can measure; Assemblies are invalidated by recorded workspace change rather than by wall-clock expiry, so correctness does not depend on a timeout"
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: high
confidence: medium
